 wrote about the millers'' families.","learn_more":"Nella Sorrow (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.dly.11","format":"mc","category":"soc","stem":"Which fixture holiday closes the Pellin mills for a day?","options":["Flour Day","Bridge Day","Salt Day","Tide Night"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"On Flour Day the mills stop and the town bakes bread for every household.","learn_more":"Flour Day (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.dly.12","format":"mc","category":"geo","stem":"Which fixture hill overlooks the town of Pellin?","options":["Beacon Knoll","Grey Tor","Crow Hill","Ash Mound"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"A fire basket on Beacon Knoll once warned the mills of floods upstream.","learn_more":"Beacon Knoll (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.dly.13","format":"mc","category":"food","stem":"Which fixture drink is brewed from Pellin heather?","options":["Heather ale","Juniper gin","Plum wine","Birch mead"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"Brewers steep heather tips in the wort, which gives the ale a honeyed scent.","learn_more":"Heather ale (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.dly.14","format":"mc","category":"hist","stem":"In which year did the fixture mills of Pellin burn?","options":["1641","1588","1702","1766"],"correct":0,"option_order":"ascending","value_display":null,"explanation":"A dry summer and a spark from a millstone set the whole row alight in 1641.","learn_more":"Pellin mills (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.fx-party.01","format":"mc","category":"soc","stem":"Which fixture game is played at every Cindral wedding?","options":["Ring toss","Tug of war","Hopscotch","Blind man''s buff"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"Guests toss rope rings over a pole hung with ribbons.","learn_more":"Cindral weddings (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.fx-party.02","format":"mc","category":"food","stem":"What is the fixture breakfast of a Gorlund sailor?","options":["Kipper and oats","Bread and lard","Eggs and kale","Rice and fish"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"A smoked kipper over oats keeps a sailor going through a cold watch.","learn_more":"Gorlund breakfast (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.fx-party.03","format":"mc","category":"music","stem":"Which fixture band plays the Halvessa harbour on Bridge Day?","options":["Halvessa Brass","The Copper Owls","Northbridge","Fen Hollow"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"The brass band marches the harbour wall each Bridge Day.","learn_more":"Halvessa Brass (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.fx-party.04","format":"mc","category":"geo","stem":"Which fixture headland shelters the harbour of Gorlund?","options":["Seal Point","Gull Ness","Black Head","Long Spit"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"Seal Point curls around the harbour and breaks the winter swell.","learn_more":"Seal Point (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.fx-party.05","format":"mc","category":"nat","stem":"Which fixture animal guards the Gorlund sheepfolds?","options":["A grey goose","A black dog","A red fox","A white llama"],"correct":0,"option_order":"shuffle","value_display":null,"explanation":"Gorlund farmers keep geese that hiss at any stranger.","learn_more":"Gorlund geese (fixture)","review_by":null,"status":"active"},{"id":"fx.r.fx-party.06","format":"mc","category":"sport","stem":"How long is the fixture Gorlund rowing race?","options":["4 km","1 km","9 km","15 km"],"correct":0,"option_order":"ascending","value_display":null,"explanation":"Crews row four kilometres from the bridge to the harbour mouth.","learn_more":"Gorlund 